      {"t":"order","p":"They're going to take the train.","a":["Ils","vont","prendre","le","train."],"x":["va"],"why":"Ils takes the ils form of aller, vont; prendre stays in the infinitive."},
      {"t":"order","p":"We're going to leave. (use nous)","a":["Nous","allons","partir."],"x":["vont"],"why":"The nous form of aller is allons."},
      {"t":"order","p":"I'm going to book a hotel.","a":["Je","vais","réserver","un","hôtel."],"x":["à"],"why":"No à between aller and the infinitive: je vais réserver."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"Elle va __ ce soir.","p":"She's going to arrive tonight.","a":["arriver"],"o":["arrive","arrives","à arriver"],"why":"After aller, the verb stays in the infinitive: arriver."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"Vous __ prendre l'avion?","p":"Are you going to fly? (to a stranger)","a":["allez"],"o":["vont","va","allons"],"why":"With vous, aller is allez."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"Je ne __ pas travailler demain.","p":"I'm not going to work tomorrow.","a":["vais"],"o":["va","vas","suis"],"why":"With je, aller is vais; ne … pas goes around it."},
      {"t":"type","p":"I'm going to visit Lyon.","a":["Je vais visiter Lyon."],"hint":"aller · visiter · Lyon","x":["va","visite"],"why":"The je form of aller is vais, then the infinitive visiter."},
      {"t":"type","p":"We're going to eat at Léa's. (use nous)","a":["Nous allons manger chez Léa."],"hint":"aller · manger · chez Léa","x":["vont"],"why":"The nous form of aller is allons."},
      {"t":"type","p":"This weekend, I'm going to go biking.","a":["Ce week-end, je vais faire du vélo.","Je vais faire du vélo ce week-end.","Ce weekend, je vais faire du vélo.","Je vais faire du vélo ce weekend."],"hint":"ce week-end · aller · faire du vélo","x":["fais"],"why":"In the futur proche, faire stays in the infinitive after je vais."}
