      {"t":"fill","q":"Va __ gare.","p":"Go to the train station.","a":["à la"],"o":["au","aux","à le"],"why":"gare is feminine, so à stays separate: à la gare."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"Il __ réserver une table.","p":"You need to book a table.","a":["faut"],"o":["fait","va","est"],"why":"il faut + infinitive: you need to, we need to."},
      {"t":"type","p":"Let's take the subway. (use the nous command)","a":["Prenons le métro."],"hint":"prendre · le métro","x":["Prends","Prenez"],"why":"Let's is the nous form: the verb ending is -ons, Prenons."},
      {"t":"type","p":"Turn right. (to a stranger)","a":["Tournez à droite."],"hint":"tourner · à droite","x":["Tourne"],"why":"To a stranger, use the vous form: Tournez, with the verb ending -ez."},
      {"t":"type","p":"Go to the museum. (to a friend)","a":["Va au musée."],"hint":"aller · le musée · tu command","x":["Vas","à"],"why":"aller drops its -s in a tu command, and à + le contracts to au: Va au musée."}
