      {"t":"mc","q":"Tu vas à la gare? 'Yes, I'm going.' =","o":["Oui, j'y vais.","Oui, je vais.","Oui, j'en vais.","Oui, je vais y."],"why":"y replaces à + a place and goes before the verb."},
      {"t":"mc","q":"Vous voulez des pommes? 'I'd like three.' =","o":["J'en voudrais trois.","Je voudrais trois.","Je les voudrais trois.","J'y voudrais trois."],"why":"With a number and no noun, French adds en: j'en voudrais trois."},
      {"t":"order","p":"I'll take it (the jacket, la veste)","a":["Je","la","prends"],"x":["le"],"why":"veste is feminine, so the pronoun is la."},
      {"t":"order","p":"I'm going to take them (the shoes)","a":["Je","vais","les","prendre"],"x":["le"],"why":"chaussures is plural, so the pronoun takes the plural form les, before the infinitive."},
      {"t":"order","p":"I'm not taking it (the sweater, le pull)","a":["Je","ne","le","prends","pas"],"x":["la"],"why":"pull is masculine: le, inside ne … pas."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"La robe? Je __achète.","p":"The dress? I'll buy it.","a":["l'"],"o":["le","la","lui"],"why":"la becomes l' before a vowel: je l'achète."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"Tu parles à Léa? Oui, je __ parle.","p":"Are you talking to Léa? Yes, I'm talking to her.","a":["lui"],"o":["la","le","leur"],"why":"parler à takes lui: to her."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"Il y a du pain? Oui, il y __ a.","p":"Is there any bread? Yes, there is.","a":["en"],"o":["le","y","lui"],"why":"en replaces du + noun: il y en a."},
      {"t":"type","p":"I'll take it. (la chemise)","a":["Je la prends.","Je vais la prendre."],"hint":"prendre · la chemise","x":["le"],"why":"chemise is feminine, so the pronoun agrees: la."},
      {"t":"type","p":"We're going to buy them. (les chaussures; use nous)","a":["Nous allons les acheter."],"hint":"aller · acheter · les chaussures","x":["allez","le"],"why":"nous takes the nous form, allons, and les is the plural form for chaussures."},
      {"t":"type","p":"I'm calling them. (mes parents; use téléphoner)","a":["Je leur téléphone."],"hint":"téléphoner à · mes parents","x":["les"],"why":"téléphoner takes à, so to them is leur."}
